{
  "info": {
    "name": "ZATCA API \u2014 test site (zatca-test)",
    "_postman_id": "e2f4a6b8-1c3d-4e5f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b",
    "description": "# ZATCA API \u2014 test site\n\nPre-configured for the **`zatca-test.enfonoerp.com`** test site on EFTSD-002 (`185.193.19.184`), seeded with company **ZATCA Test Co** (SAR, 15% VAT) and **ZATCA Phase 1** active.\n\n## Before you run anything\n\n1. Select the **ZATCA API \u2014 test site** environment.\n2. Paste `api_key` and `api_secret` (they are deliberately blank \u2014 never stored in the repo). Get them by re-running the seeder on the server:\n   `bench --site zatca-test.enfonoerp.com console` then\n   `from zatca_api.setup_test_site import run; run()`\n   The secret is only recoverable at creation, so a re-run issues a new one.\n3. Set `base_url` \u2014 see below.\n4. Run **01 Ping**. Everything else assumes it passed.\n\n## Reaching the site\n\nThe server side is done \u2014 nginx on `185.193.19.184` has a server block for\n`zatca-test.enfonoerp.com` and routes it to the right site. Verified end to end.\n\nWhat is missing is **DNS**: `zatca-test.enfonoerp.com` still resolves to Cloudflare, not\nto the server. Until a record exists, make your own machine resolve it:\n\n```\nsudo sh -c 'echo \"185.193.19.184  zatca-test.enfonoerp.com\" >> /etc/hosts'\n```\n\nThen `base_url = http://zatca-test.enfonoerp.com` works immediately, in both Postman and\nthe browser.\n\nFor everyone (and for HTTPS), add a DNS A record `zatca-test -> 185.193.19.184`,\n**DNS-only / grey cloud**, exactly like `misk-dev.enfonoerp.com`. Then certbot can issue\na cert and `base_url` becomes `https://...`.\n\n**`http://185.193.19.184` on its own will not work.** The box has no `default_server`, so\na request whose Host matches nothing falls through to the first server block and is\nserved as a different site \u2014 that is what produced \"App zatca_api is not installed\". The\nhostname has to be right.\n\nEvery request also carries `X-Frappe-Site-Name`, which helps when a request does not\narrive on the site's own hostname, and is harmless when it does.\n\n## Run them in order\n\nLater requests reuse `external_id` and `last_invoice` captured by earlier ones. Requests 03, 12 and 13 are **meant** to fail \u2014 they prove the error handling.\n\n## Expected numbers on this site\n\n| Request | Expect |\n| --- | --- |\n| 02 dry run | net 500, VAT 75, grand **575 SAR**, `valid: true` |\n| 03 B2B no address | `valid: false`, address named |\n| 04 B2C create | grand **575**, `phase: Phase 1`, QR ~1100-1600 bytes |\n| 06 B2B create | grand **5175**, **warnings empty** |\n| 07 mixed VAT | net 2000, VAT **150** (not 300) |\n| 08 credit note | `is_return: 1`, qty negative |\n\nFull reference: `docs/USER_GUIDE.md`. Spec for whoever builds the feed: `docs/DATA_CONTRACT.md`.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
